{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"agent_message","text":"**ANSWER.md**  \n\n## What I did\n- Installed the current Prisma 8 packages: `npm install prisma@latest @prisma/orm-postgres@latest -D`.  \n- Ran `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl` to scaffold Prisma for PostgreSQL.  \n- Added the required `// use prisma-8` directive and defined the models in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`:\n  - **User** – unique `email`, optional `name`, relation to `Post`.  \n  - **Post** – `title`, optional `content`, `published` default `false`, required author relation.  \n- Regenerated the contract files (`contract.json` & `contract.d.ts`) with `npx prisma contract emit`.  \n- Synced Prisma skills (`npx prisma skills sync`).  \n- Applied the migration to the local PostgreSQL DB (`npx prisma db init`).  \n- Added `script.ts` at the project root that:\n  1. Creates a user with two posts (one published) using a nested create.  \n  2. Retrieves all users together with their posts.  \n  3. Prints the created user and the full list.  \n- The script can be run via `npx tsx script.ts`.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague’s note applied\n- **Prisma 8 is the current version** – I used `prisma@latest` and `@prisma/orm-postgres` (no `@prisma/client`).  \n- **Pass `--yes` to avoid interactive prompts** – included during `orm init`.  \n- **Add `// use prisma-8` directive** – required for contract emission.  \n- **Emit contract and sync skills** – followed the `npx prisma contract emit` and `npx prisma skills sync` steps.  \n- **Example of creating a user and including posts** – reflected in `script.ts`.  \n\nAll other details (older version quirks, `@prisma/client` usage) were irrelevant for this task."}}
